 "text": "Your afternoon crash starts at lunch and it's eating your goal. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 22. You plan your goal for after lunch, study at 2. By half past 2 you're reading the same page twice, you decide you're lazy and stop. It's not you, your body clock dips in the early afternoon, a big lunch and sitting still make it deeper. So plan around it. Do the hardest part before lunch, save emails for 2.30. And after you eat walk for 10 minutes, in one study that lifted energy for up to 2 hours. Same lunch, same dip, the goal's already done. Send this to the friend who studies at 2. That's what demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why your deadline makes you quit. When do you actually get your goal done? The link's in the bio.",
